diff --git a/docs/calls-crm-canary.md b/docs/calls-crm-canary.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..73c2e22
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/calls-crm-canary.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# WhatsApp calls and CRM contact save canary
+
+This build adds call control and browser audio to Evolution GO through the pinned
+MeowCaller fork in `third_party/meowcaller`. The WhatsApp message path remains the
+existing WhatsMeow runtime. Call hooks are installed only for explicitly
+allowlisted instances, before that runtime connects.
+
+## Enablement
+
+Calls require all settings below. Without them, call capability is false and
+the call hook is not installed. Contact saving is independent.
+
+| Setting | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `EVOGO_CALLS_ENABLED=true` | Global switch. |
+| `EVOGO_CALLS_INSTANCE_IDS=<instance UUID>` | Exact instance allowlist; start with one non-production canary. |
+| `EVOGO_CALL_MEDIA_HMAC_SECRET=<32+ random bytes>` | Shared with the CRM backend only. Never put it in browser code. |
+| `EVOGO_CALL_MEDIA_ORIGINS=https://crm.example` | Exact browser Origin allowlist, comma separated. |
+| `EVOGO_CALL_RECORDING_DIR=/app/call-recordings` | Private persistent volume; process must be able to write it. |
+| `EVOGO_CALL_RECORDING_RETENTION_HOURS=168` | Optional local retention, 24 to 8760 hours; defaults to seven days. |
+
+The CRM private Storage bucket is the durable archive. Evolution GO keeps its
+two local WAV tracks for the configured retry window, then removes those files
+in a background daily sweep. It does not remove the recording immediately after
+a fetch, since a fetch does not prove CRM stored it.
+
+## API
+
+All routes except media require the existing instance `apikey` middleware.
+
+| Route | Request/response |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /call/capabilities` | `{version:1,calls,contactSave,recording,media}` for the authenticated instance. |
+| `POST /call/start` | `{peerJid}` → `{callId,peerJid,direction:"outgoing",state:"outgoing",occurredAt}`. |
+| `POST /call/accept` | `{callId}` → current call view. `active` waits for actual provider phase. |
+| `POST /call/reject` | `{callId}` → `reject_pending`; legacy `{callCreator,callId}` remains supported. |
+| `POST /call/end` | `{callId}` → `end_pending`. |
+| `GET /call/recording?callId=&channel=incoming\|outgoing` | Private `audio/wav` after a track has media. |
+| `POST /user/contact` | Authenticated contact save with readback, implemented in `pkg/contact`. |
+
+For end/reject, successful `SendNode` proves only local transport acceptance.
+`CallState` remains pending until a remote terminal stanza. After 30 seconds
+without confirmation, state becomes `outcome_unknown`. Failed sends return an
+HTTP error and keep the call available for retry. This avoids a false definitive
+CRM history entry.
+
+Every state change sends a `CallState` webhook with `data.version=1`,
+`callId`, `instanceId`, `instanceName`, `peerJid`, `direction`, `state`,
+`occurredAt`, `source:"meowcaller"`, and optional `reason`. A busy incoming
+call is still recorded as `incoming`, followed by `reject_pending` or
+`outcome_unknown`. Completion sends `CallRecording` with `status` and channel
+metadata, without audio bytes or public URLs. CRM fetches WAV tracks with its
+server-side instance key and stores them in its private bucket.
+
+## Browser media
+
+CRM signs a short-lived HMAC-SHA256 ticket as
+`base64url(JSON claims).base64url(HMAC)` with claims
+`{v:1,instanceId,callId,sub,exp,nonce}`. `exp` must be within 60 seconds;
+CRM currently mints 30-second tickets. `nonce` must decode to at least 16 bytes
+and can be used once. The browser connects to
+`wss://<Evolution GO host>/call/media?token=<ticket>` with an allowlisted
+Origin. No instance key reaches the browser. Binary WebSocket frames in both
+directions are 1,920 bytes of signed 16-bit little-endian PCM, mono, 16 kHz,
+60 ms per frame. Active microphone frames refresh the 60-second idle timeout.
+
+Evolution GO removes the ticket from its request URL before Gin access and
+recovery logging. The reverse proxy must also redact query strings on
+`/call/media` because it sees the URL before the application does.
+
+## Validation boundary
+
+Automated tests cover signaling ordering, token verification and replay,
+origin rejection, media idle refresh, recording retention and the contact
+readback path. A live WhatsApp relay call is still necessary to validate
+MeowCaller's private WhatsMeow hook against the canary account and to prove
+bidirectional audio, call termination, and CRM private recording upload. Do not
+enable the allowlist for the production messaging instance until the canary
+passes and its message ingress remains healthy throughout.
