new file mode 100644
index 0000000..973fcc3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pkg/contact/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# WhatsApp contact write
+
+`POST /user/contact` writes a name to the WhatsApp account linked to the authenticated Evolution GO instance. Register `contact_handler.NewHandler(contact_service.NewService(whatsmeowService)).Save` inside the existing `/user` group protected by `Auth`.
+
+Request: `{"number":"5511999999999","fullName":"Maria Silva"}`. The number must include its country code, optionally prefixed by `+` or suffixed by `@s.whatsapp.net`. Other JID domains, device JIDs, groups, and unformatted local phone numbers are rejected.
+
+The service uses the current authorized WhatsMeow runtime only. It sends the contact `SET` mutation in `critical_unblock_low`, then reads the synchronized contact name from that same runtime's store. A 200 response means this linked session read the requested name after the server accepted the patch. A 502 response is intentionally inconclusive: the patch may have been accepted even if readback failed. Retrying the same name is safe as a `SET` mutation.
+
+This does **not** confirm that the native Contacts app on the paired phone changed. Verify WhatsApp mobile display and native phone address book separately with a test account before enabling the CRM button broadly. It also does not create or update any CRM lead/contact record; the CRM endpoint must decide which organization, lead, and Evo instance the action belongs to.
